vllm.cpp: DFlash draft weights staged to device at load (5 layers)
vllm.cpp: VT_DFLASH_DRAFT=1 — the DFlash2 draft proposes through the DIRECT-ARGMAX arm (bundle dflash2.py has_selector=false): full-vocab argmax per block row, candidate selector NOT resident (~254 MB freed). The verify stays lossless (greedy accept = the target's argmax); only acceptance can differ from the selector arm.
vllm.cpp: draft speculative context is limited to 592 tokens (37 pages x 16, 11.5625 MiB per concurrent request across 5 draft layers, so 11.5625 MiB of device memory at max_num_seqs 1 — NOT counted by gpu_memory_utilization). max_model_len is 576 and the (1+k) draft block needs 9 more, so the whole advertised context is speculated.
vllm.cpp: Asynchronous scheduling is disabled (max_concurrent_batches=1)
